  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Fantasy Football Sign-Up Sheet FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a fantasy football sign up sheet?\", \"a\": \"A fantasy football sign up sheet is the form a commissioner sends before the season to collect each manager's name, team name, and contact email for the league invite. A league can put keeper picks, draft-night availability, and a scoring vote on the same sheet.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a fantasy football sign up sheet?\", \"a\": \"Tell Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> about the league in plain English: the team cap, what each manager answers, and any keeper or draft-night section. Emergent builds the sheet and a database for the answers. Run two test entries, then share the link with the league.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a fantasy football sign up sheet ask?\", \"a\": \"Ask for the manager's name, a team name, and an email address for the league app's invite. Add a phone number if the league talks by text. Returning leagues add keepers, and new leagues add a draft-night poll. Keep the first page to those basics so nobody quits halfway.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I cap the number of managers on a fantasy football sign up sheet?\", \"a\": \"Put a team cap on the sign-up sheet. Once the cap is reached, the sheet stops seating new managers and lists each later sign-up on a waitlist by arrival time. When a seated manager drops out, offer the seat to the first name on that list.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I collect keeper picks on a fantasy football sign up sheet?\", \"a\": \"Add a keeper section that only returning managers fill in, with a limit on how many players each can name. Ask for the player's name and position for each keeper. Set the due date a week before the draft to leave time to sort out disputes.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a fantasy football sign up sheet poll managers on a draft night?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Give each night its own question with the start time attached, and let managers answer all of them. Count the yes votes per night and pick the highest. Announce the winner to the whole league by email, and put the date on the sheet's confirmation page for late joiners.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a fantasy football sign up sheet include a scoring vote?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when scoring is still open. ESPN's help center says that in a PPR league, players who catch a reception earn a point, while standard leagues do not award a point for a catch. Close the vote before the draft.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I send reminders from a fantasy football sign up sheet?\", \"a\": \"Set a sign-up deadline and send an email reminder two days before it to anyone on last season's list who has not answered. The app Emergent builds can send that email on a schedule and show the commissioner who is still missing.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where do fantasy football sign up sheet answers get stored?\", \"a\": \"Every answer lands as a row in one table: one row per manager, with team name, email, keepers, and draft-night votes. With Emergent, that table sits in a database you own, and no response caps cut off a big league partway through sign-ups.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I reuse a fantasy football sign up sheet next season?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Keep last season's managers in the table and send them the same link with this year's dates. Change the questions by prompt when the league adds a keeper or switches scoring. On paid plans, the full code can be exported to your GitHub repository.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}